  "lineage": "Late-2000s indie-electronic subgenre developed through internet-distributed-production scene, characterized by hazy-reverbed atmospheric production, 1980s-synth-and-disco sampling, mid-tempo languid grooves, and explicit nostalgic-summer-evening aesthetic. Washed Out, Toro y Moi, Neon Indian, and Ducktails inaugurated the canonical sound c. 2009-2011; the broader Carpark Records, Mexican Summer, and Captured Tracks label rosters anchored institutional infrastructure.",
